Test the default root endpoint to verify it returns the expected message.

**Step 1:** With the application running, test using curl:
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000
```
Expected response:
```text
Hello World!
```

**Step 2:** Verify the controller logic in `app.controller.ts`:
```typescript
@Controller()
export class AppController {
  constructor(private readonly appService: AppService) {}

  @Get()
  getHello(): string {
    return this.appService.getHello();
  }
}
```

**Note:** The default scaffolded project already includes this endpoint. Ensure `AppController` and `AppService` are properly registered in `AppModule`. Read more at [NestJS Controllers](https://docs.nestjs.com/controllers).
